{"id":15423,"date":"2023-05-18T14:23:36","date_gmt":"2023-05-18T20:23:36","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/www.rethinkbehavioralhealth.com\/?post_type=resources&#038;p=15423"},"modified":"2023-10-20T16:59:22","modified_gmt":"2023-10-20T22:59:22","slug":"supporting-more-positive-quality-life-autistic-adolescents-adults","status":"publish","type":"resources","link":"https:\/\/www.rethinkbehavioralhealth.com\/resources\/supporting-more-positive-quality-life-autistic-adolescents-adults\/","title":{"rendered":"Supporting a More Positive Quality of Life for Autistic Adolescents and Adults"},"content":{"rendered":"\t\t<div data-elementor-type=\"wp-post\" data-elementor-id=\"15423\" class=\"elementor elementor-15423\" data-elementor-post-type=\"resources\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<section class=\"elementor-section elementor-top-section elementor-element elementor-element-c65705b elementor-section-boxed elementor-section-height-default elementor-section-height-default\" data-id=\"c65705b\" data-element_type=\"section\" data-settings=\"{&quot;jet_parallax_layout_list&quot;:[]}\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-container elementor-column-gap-default\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-column elementor-col-100 elementor-top-column elementor-element elementor-element-f4ca00d\" data-id=\"f4ca00d\" data-element_type=\"column\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-wrap elementor-element-populated\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-ec2b97b elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"ec2b97b\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<h2 style=\"margin-top: 0;\">About this Webinar<\/h2><p>Dr. Bridget Taylor hosts Dr. Peter Gerhardt to discuss how behavior analysts can promote Quality of Life, a complex yet important measure in autism treatment, for their clients throughout their lifetime.<\/p><p><em><strong>This webinar is eligible for 1 General CE.<\/strong><\/em><\/p><p><a href=\"https:\/\/behaviorlive.com\/courses\/supporting-a-more-positive-quality-of-life-for-autistic-adolescents-and-adults\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>View On-Demand Webinar<\/strong><\/a><\/p><h3>Our Next Guest: A Conversation with Drs. Bridget Taylor &amp; Peter Gerhardt<\/h3><p>Promoting a positive quality of life is something that certainly falls within the parameters of behavior analytic intervention and socially significant outcomes. To make this happen, however, the development of meaningful instructional goals and the identification of relevant environmental modifications needs to start in elementary school and continue into transition, graduation and beyond. As with most, if not all of what competent behavior analysts do, this process is highly individualized and requires programming for both generalization and maintenance.<\/p><h2>Learning Objectives<\/h2><p>At the conclusion of the presentation, participants will be able to:<\/p><ol><li>Discuss the difficulty in identifying the parameters of quality of life on a case-by-case basis.<\/li><li>Identify a minimum of 5 personal or ecological parameters associated with a more positive quality of life.<\/li><li>Identify behaviorally-based strategies that may improve an individual\u2019s quality of life.<\/li><\/ol><h2>About the Guest Speaker<\/h2>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<\/section>\n\t\t\t\t<section class=\"elementor-section elementor-top-section elementor-element elementor-element-1b31e2a authorSection elementor-section-boxed elementor-section-height-default elementor-section-height-default\" data-id=\"1b31e2a\" data-element_type=\"section\" data-settings=\"{&quot;jet_parallax_layout_list&quot;:[]}\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-container elementor-column-gap-default\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-column elementor-col-33 elementor-top-column elementor-element elementor-element-526c319\" data-id=\"526c319\" data-element_type=\"column\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-wrap elementor-element-populated\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-b63835f elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\" data-id=\"b63835f\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"image.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<img fetchpriority=\"high\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"600\" height=\"600\" src=\"https:\/\/www.rethinkbehavioralhealth.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/05\/dr-peter-gerhardt-our-next-guest-rethinkbh.jpg\" class=\"attachment-full size-full wp-image-15381\" alt=\"Dr. Peter Gerhardt\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.rethinkbehavioralhealth.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/05\/dr-peter-gerhardt-our-next-guest-rethinkbh.jpg 600w, https:\/\/www.rethinkbehavioralhealth.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/05\/dr-peter-gerhardt-our-next-guest-rethinkbh-300x300.jpg 300w, https:\/\/www.rethinkbehavioralhealth.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/05\/dr-peter-gerhardt-our-next-guest-rethinkbh-150x150.jpg 150w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 600px) 100vw, 600px\" \/>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-column elementor-col-66 elementor-top-column elementor-element elementor-element-7e23c53\" data-id=\"7e23c53\" data-element_type=\"column\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-wrap elementor-element-populated\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-6e332b4 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"6e332b4\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<h3>Peter Gerhardt, Ed.D<\/h3><p><span style=\"color: #333333;\">Executive Director of the EPIC Programs<\/span><\/p><p>Dr. Gerhardt is the Executive Director of the\u00a0<a href=\"https:\/\/www.epicschool.org\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">EPIC Programs<\/a> in Paramus, NJ. Dr. Gerhardt has over 40 years of experience utilizing the principles of Applied Behavior Analysis in support of adolescents and adults with autism spectrum disorders in educational, employment, residential and community-based settings. He co-edited <em>\u201cThe Handbook of Quality of Life for Individuals with ASD\u201d<\/em> (Springer, 2022) and authored or co-author a number of articles and book chapters on the needs of adolescents and adults with ASD. He has presented nationally and internationally on this and related topics. Dr. Gerhardt serves as Co-Chairman of the Scientific Council for the Organization for Autism Research and is on numerous professional advisory boards including the Cambridge Center for Behavioral Studies. He currently serves as adjunct faculty in the Institute for Behavioral Studies at Endicott College. Dr. Gerhardt received his doctorate from Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey\u2019s Graduate School of Education.<\/p>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<\/section>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t","protected":false},"author":19,"featured_media":15426,"template":"","meta":{"_seopress_robots_primary_cat":"","_seopress_titles_title":"Support for Positive Quality of Life: Autistic Kids &amp; Adults","_seopress_titles_desc":"On-demand webinar, eligible for 1 General CE, of difficulty identifying parameters of quality of life on case-by-case basis and personal\/ecological parameters.","_seopress_robots_index":"","om_disable_all_campaigns":false,"_links_to":"","_links_to_target":""},"audience":[70],"resource-type":[72],"resource-topic":[97,329],"resource-tag":[287,174,103,346,339],"class_list":["post-15423","resources","type-resources","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","audience-providers","resource-type-webinar","resource-topic-autism","resource-topic-behavior","resource-tag-continuing-education","resource-tag-goals","resource-tag-objective","resource-tag-quality-of-life","resource-tag-success"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/www.rethinkbehavioralhealth.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/resources\/15423","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/www.rethinkbehavioralhealth.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/resources"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/www.rethinkbehavioralhealth.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/resources"}],"author":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/www.rethinkbehavioralhealth.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/users\/19"}],"version-history":[{"count":0,"href":"https:\/\/www.rethinkbehavioralhealth.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/resources\/15423\/revisions"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/www.rethinkbehavioralhealth.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media\/15426"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/www.rethinkbehavioralhealth.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=15423"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"audience","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/www.rethinkbehavioralhealth.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/audience?post=15423"},{"taxonomy":"resource-type","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/www.rethinkbehavioralhealth.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/resource-type?post=15423"},{"taxonomy":"resource-topic","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/www.rethinkbehavioralhealth.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/resource-topic?post=15423"},{"taxonomy":"resource-tag","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/www.rethinkbehavioralhealth.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/resource-tag?post=15423"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}}